1
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:42,660
It'll be fine somehow.

2
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:45,960
You understand, right?

3
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,920
I know, I know.

4
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:51,800
If you understand, shut up and follow me.

5
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:07,800
Ryotsu Prank – Top Secret Report

6
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:12,140
He's coming! Get a closer shot!

7
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:12,740
Yes.

8
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:17,880
The police officer in sandals with the thick,
connected eyebrows.

9
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:21,100
No mistake, it was in the tip from a viewer.

10
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:23,000
He's the police officer named Ryotsu.

11
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:25,320
Is the setup all right?

12
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,340
It's all set, no problem.

13
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:30,340
There are 325 fake gold koban
we brought from the studio.

14
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:31,460
They're all placed properly.

15
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:35,180
When he picks up the koban,
if we go out holding this placard,

16
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:37,600
So the shoot wraps up happily, right?

17
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:41,020
Do you think it'll work?

18
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:45,760
Don't worry, he's said to be
extremely greedy and crazy about money.

19
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,180
I saw it.

20
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,680
Okay, just like that, just like that.

21
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:59,080
He walked right past them.

22
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:01,660
That's strange.
Why didn't he pick up the koban?

23
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:06,660
The koban are gone.

24
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:08,000
When did that happen?

25
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,040
No way.

26
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,500
Here it is.

27
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:15,100
Stop.

28
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:19,680
There's nothing suspicious here, is there?

29
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:22,060
Now I'll play it in slow motion.

30
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:29,160
As expected, nothing unusual is visible.

31
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:31,160
Next, I'll try advancing it frame by frame.

32
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:37,980
What?

33
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,260
Only this one frame shows him.

34
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,300
He's incredibly fast!

35
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:45,720
This is no time to be impressed.

36
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,760
Hurry, go after him and hold up the placard.

37
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:48,900
We need to get the closing shot.

38
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:49,840
Right.

39
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,060
I found something good.

40
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:55,760
From the god Placid.

41
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,020
It's a reward for me.

42
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:57,840
That's right, that's right.

43
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,640
It must be.

44
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,420
This feel...

45
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:07,180
Living really does pay off sometimes.

46
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:08,320
Thank you, gods!

47
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:11,320
Ryo-san, what are you doing?

48
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,100
What's up, Terai-kun?

49
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,800
You seem pretty happy.

50
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,040
Did something good happen?

51
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:20,020
What, what, what is he going on about?

52
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:21,840
Terai-kun's acting strange.

53
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:23,540
Yeah.

54
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:25,020
That's right.

55
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:26,460
Ryo-san, want to eat this?

56
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:28,080
What is this?

57
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:30,040
It's koban-yaki.

58
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:32,220
Hey, what? It's a koban!

59
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:34,260
Bite-sized ōban-yaki.

60
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,960
I said it's koban-yaki.

61
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:36,720
Want one?

62
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,780
W-what's with this contrived development?

63
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:43,420
N-no way,
does this guy know about the koban?

64
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:46,320
Terai still has loan payments left, right?

65
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:48,580
Heh, I know, you know.

66
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:50,800
Quietly hand over the koban.

67
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:53,440
I won't fall for that.

68
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:56,040
Even if you shift the setup,
it won't work on me.

69
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,440
Uh... yeah.

70
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,340
Ryo-san's acting weird.

71
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:04,040
That was close.

72
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:07,740
Ugh, even if they're colleagues, when it
comes to money, that's a whole different story.

73
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:08,880
I have to be careful.

74
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:12,560
W-who's watching me? Am I just imagining it?

75
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:14,240
No, I can definitely feel it.

76
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:17,860
So, I'm the one with the koban

77
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,140
K-koban?

78
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,980
Koban-san, Koban-san.

79
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:21,700
Koban?

80
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:24,340
Koban and a big job.

81
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:25,220
Koban?

82
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:26,540
I'd love to do that.

83
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:37,440
Pearls before swine. Could these guys be fakes too? After all,
I'm rich!

84
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:42,640
There he is!

85
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:45,300
Alright, let's go with the catchphrase!

86
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:49,180
Too bad! It's the Surprise Camera!

87
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:56,020
We caught such a decisive moment,
we can't end the show without showing this.

88
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:59,680
Damn it!
We're catching him no matter what! Hurry!

89
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:04,540
Just as I thought, he's here!
But I'll protect the koban no matter what!

90
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:12,320
There he is!

91
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:17,400
Too bad! Surprise!

92
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:18,740
Damn!

93
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:23,940
Damn it! Where did he go?

94
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,060
Over there!

95
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:29,600
Aaaaah! Too bad, yeah!

96
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:32,780
W-wait, hold on!

97
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:41,040
Where'd he go? There!

98
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:52,120
Yes! This time we've got him. Alright, here we go!
Too bad, it's the Surprise Camera!

99
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:58,840
I'm definitely not giving up these koban!

100
00:05:59,420 --> 00:05:59,780
No way...

101
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:07,260
What?

102
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:10,060
You set up a Surprise Camera on Ryotsu?

103
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:10,800
Yes.

104
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:13,300
We received a postcard from a viewer,

105
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:14,940
and it said something quite outrageous.

106
00:06:14,940 --> 00:06:15,680
No, no.

107
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,060
We heard there's an
eccentric police officer here,

108
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:20,220
and we wanted to film him finding

109
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,240
a fake gold koban.

110
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:27,080
But Mr. Ryotsu snatched
it up in no time at all,

111
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:30,220
and we can't end the
show without showing this.

112
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:32,040
Please, somehow catch him.

113
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:36,020
But did Ryotsu really take the koban?

114
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:38,700
Sure, he's an idiot and a total mess,

115
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:41,380
a greedy, worthless police officer,

116
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:44,120
but pocketing something he found on the ground?
That's a bit much.

117
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:46,160
He just might.

118
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:48,480
We also have conclusive evidence.

119
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:49,780
This is it.

120
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:55,040
Even though we expected it,

121
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,680
I never thought he'd actually pocket it.

122
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,000
Damn you, Ryotsu!

123
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:03,340
I tried to trust you, just a little, out of
fatherly affection, and you've wasted it all.

124
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:04,260
Let's go!

125
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,300
Go where?

126
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:09,140
Where would Ryotsu go
now that he has the koban?

127
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:10,600
I've already figured that out.

128
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:17,080
Looks like those guys gave up.

129
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,160
Hehehehehe.

130
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:22,740
Well then,
time to cash in these koban without a worry.

131
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:24,460
Here we go!

132
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:25,360
Hey, wait!

133
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,360
C-C-Chief!

134
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,200
What are you doing in a place like this?

135
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,460
N-no, well, nothing in particular.

136
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:37,120
Do you have business at this antique shop?

137
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:40,680
Um, I didn't know there
was an antique shop here.

138
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,180
I had no idea.

139
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:46,000
Apparently some people these days think
nothing of selling things they've picked up.

140
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:50,960
Especially someone who picks up a koban and
tries to sell it is completely out of line!

141
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:53,900
Yes, you're right, Chief.
Exactly as you say.

142
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:57,100
Are you hiding something from me?

143
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:59,180
No, nothing at all.

144
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:02,880
If you apologize now,
I might just forgive you as a special favor.

145
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:05,660
What are you talking about? I have no idea.

146
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:08,320
Really?
You really haven't done anything, have you?

147
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:14,720
Of course! Ryo-chan, the poor, law-abiding,
pure, and spotless Buddha, that's me!

148
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:20,120
Don't play dumb! We've already confirmed
that you pocketed the koban you found!

149
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:21,180
Hey!

150
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:21,920
Look!

151
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,580
Too bad!

152
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:27,120
It's a Surprise Camera!

153
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:30,860
So that means these koban are...

154
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:33,140
All fake!

155
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:37,300
Fake?

156
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:42,480
What?! That's awful!

157
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,220
Setting someone up like that!

158
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:46,540
You two really went and did it, didn't you?

159
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:47,820
You idiot!

160
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:50,300
It all started when you
tried to pocket a lost item.

161
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:51,440
It's your own fault, you know!

162
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:53,860
And on top of that,
you played dumb right up to the very end.

163
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:56,080
I absolutely will not forgive you this time.

164
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:59,100
Damn it!

165
00:08:59,100 --> 00:09:01,040
You're certainly quick on your feet.

166
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:02,120
Thank you very much.

167
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:05,120
With this, we're bound to get great ratings.

168
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:06,620
About that...

169
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:09,460
Is there any way we could skip airing this?

170
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:12,260
If this gets broadcast,

171
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:14,560
our station's disgrace will
be exposed across the nation.

172
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:16,520
But it's sure to be a hit.

173
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:19,040
We'll blur the faces, so it'll be fine.

174
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:20,340
Excuse me.

175
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:21,720
Yes, hello?

176
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:25,120
N-no way...

177
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,520
What happened?

178
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:30,160
The koban you brought in is
apparently the real thing.

179
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:34,320
It was scheduled to be appraised on
next week's treasure appraisal show.

180
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:37,020
Apparently it was swapped
with a genuine koban.

181
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:38,640
Just now, on the phone...

182
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:42,840
Yes.

183
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:48,340
All of these are fake.
If they were real, by now...

184
00:09:48,340 --> 00:09:49,040
Ryo-san!

185
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:50,720
It's you two.

186
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:51,860
Hey, hey, what's that?

187
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:55,380
This is, well, a fake koban.

188
00:09:55,680 --> 00:09:57,080
A fake koban?

189
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,580
Yeah, if you want some,
I'll give them to you.

190
00:09:58,920 --> 00:09:59,780
Yay!

191
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,340
Which one!

192
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,440
Wow, that's awesome!

193
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,260
It really flies well. Alright, me too.

194
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:14,740
Come on, Ryo-san.

195
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,660
If it's this kind of thing, leave it to me.

196
00:10:17,660 --> 00:10:19,680
Here, I'll hand out koban by the bucketload.

197
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:20,440
That's right.

198
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,420
Got it!

199
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:30,780
Where did Ryotsu go?

200
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:31,960
You've got to be kidding.

201
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:34,400
If we lose the real koban,
we're fired! Fired!

202
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:36,120
I don't want that.

203
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:38,160
I still have my car loan to pay off.

204
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:42,280
I've still got 32 years
left on my house loan!

205
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,320
Ow!

206
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:49,820
Ryo-san! What about the koban from before?!

207
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:56,306
This is great! The koban's shaving off,

208
00:10:56,356 --> 00:10:58,720
and it's making golden dust!

209
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,620
Ryo-san! W-what's that?!

210
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:03,920
Hey, a fake koban? No, wait...

211
00:11:03,970 --> 00:11:06,300
Even fakes can be fun to play
with in all sorts of ways!

212
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:09,620
I handed them out to the kids,
and they were all thrilled!

213
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:14,260
You idiot!
The koban you picked up were all real!

214
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:16,940
Come on, Chief, another Surprise Camera?

215
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:19,020
I'm not falling for that again.

216
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:21,560
No! They really are real!

217
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:24,540
Really? Really?

218
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:27,320
They're genuine, appraised at ten million.

219
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:30,620
Damn it!

220
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:41,500
What have you done!

221
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:59,580
Idiot! Stay there and reflect
on what you've done for a while.

222
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:02,520
But that's not fair!
It's not my fault, right?

223
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:05,860
After all, it was the TV people
who mixed them up with the real ones.

224
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:10,520
Idiot! It's your fault for falling for some prank called
"Surprise Camera."

225
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:15,300
Pocketing the koban and handing them out to the kids,
it's all your fault!

226
00:12:15,300 --> 00:12:15,680
No way...

227
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,260
No, wait, that's no, no, no...

228
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:18,705
Honestly,

229
00:12:18,755 --> 00:12:24,440
Today, because of you,
I've been humiliated too!

230
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:26,920
I never expected you'd pocket
lost property like that.

231
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:30,780
But who'd expect anyone
to drop a koban like that?

232
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:34,020
So I figured it was a gift from the gods.

233
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:35,880
Don't talk such nonsense.

234
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:38,980
Honestly, letting yourself
get taken in by some TV stunt.

235
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:41,800
You're an idiot for falling
for something like that.

236
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:45,640
So you're saying you wouldn't
fall for a prank camera, Chief?

237
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:46,640
Of course not.

238
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:49,340
A man as cool and composed as I am

239
00:12:49,340 --> 00:12:52,340
would never fall for such an obvious setup.

240
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:53,700
Unlike you.

241
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:58,820
If you always act with pride as a police officer,
like I do,

242
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,720
you wouldn't end up in a mess like that.

243
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:03,080
Make sure you take this to heart.

244
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:04,840
I see.

245
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,540
Understood, Chief.

246
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:14,500
Welcome!

247
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:21,920
Hey, is this pot also 500 yen?

248
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:27,540
This one? That's a problem.
Grandpa still hasn't come back?

249
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:30,200
Well, fine, then it's 500 yen.

250
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:36,320
There, this is good. Wait here, okay? Achoo!

251
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:38,800
Good morning, everyone.

252
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:40,060
Good morning.

253
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:44,320
He isn't here yet?
Honestly, what a troublesome guy.

254
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:47,500
Good morning. Chief Ohara, sorry.

255
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,020
Hurry up, please. Yes!

256
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:52,340
Senpai, what's that?

257
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:55,420
It's a pot the old man from
Tsukudajima entrusted to me.

258
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:00,720
This is a weird pot.

259
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:03,560
Hah, as expected,
common folk have no eye for quality.

260
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:08,340
This was made in the Ming dynasty. In China,
it's a pot on the level of a national treasure!

261
00:14:08,340 --> 00:14:12,460
Really?
It doesn't look like anything special to me.

262
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,300
But why did you end up
looking after it, senpai?

263
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:19,080
He's apparently worried someone
will steal it if he keeps it at home.

264
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:23,380
But if I keep it at my place,
I might end up breaking it.

265
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:24,920
I suppose so.

266
00:14:25,460 --> 00:14:28,780
So, could you look after it for me, Chief?

267
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:30,680
What, me?

268
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:33,460
Terai aside,
with an eye as discerning as the Chief's,

269
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:36,260
you can tell just how
valuable this pot is, right?

270
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:41,740
If we were to break something so valuable,
historically and culturally,

271
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:44,400
we'd have no excuse to our ancestors,
would we?

272
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:48,580
Besides, this pot would surely be happier

273
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:51,260
near a connoisseur's eye like yours,
Chief, I thought.

274
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,980
Please, Chief, I beg you.

275
00:14:56,420 --> 00:14:58,500
Well, if you put it that way,
I suppose I have no choice.

276
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,260
I'll keep it here for you.

277
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:01,780
Really? Thank you so much.

278
00:15:01,780 --> 00:15:02,420
Thank you.

279
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:06,560
Phase one, success.

280
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:12,200
Alright, everyone, good work,
thanks for your effort.

281
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:27,860
Who goes there?

282
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:36,260
No matter how many times I look,
that pot doesn't look that expensive.

283
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:40,500
Don't tell me Ryotsu's
trying to pull one over on me?

284
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,720
This pot is worth ten billion yen!

285
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:44,440
What a magnificent pot.

286
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:52,740
Hey this pot is the same kind as that one. It was made in
China's Ming era and was favored by the emperor of the time,

287
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:59,160
and it's said to be a pot of noble lineage.
So if it really exists, it's definitely worth ten billion yen.

288
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:02,080
Ten billion?! I'm floored!

289
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:07,860
Ugh... this pot is worth ten billion yen?!

290
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:09,280
Here's your tea, sir.

291
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:14,000
Idiot! Call out before you come in!

292
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,280
Sorry.

293
00:16:16,260 --> 00:16:19,140
A professional appraiser says so,
so there's no mistake.

294
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:21,100
This pot is the real deal.

295
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:26,820
Phase two, successful.

296
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,380
Well, I'm off.

297
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:31,120
Yes, see you later.

298
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,040
No way.

299
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,900
It's 10 billion yen.

300
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:39,660
No way, that can't be.

301
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:41,560
Honey, what's wrong with you, honey?

302
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:45,380
Well, I'm off.

303
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:47,080
Yes, take care.

304
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:54,580
There, that's settled.

305
00:16:57,260 --> 00:17:01,500
Damn, it's starting to look
like everyone's after this pot.

306
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:03,980
And about the pot's feet, you see.

307
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,360
The pot.

308
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:07,580
That's the spot, that's the spot!

309
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,460
A tsubo button, is it?

310
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:10,020
Pot.

311
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:11,600
Isn't it a one-button one?

312
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:16,600
W-why?

313
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:18,260
Why is everyone looking at me?

314
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:19,280
Why, though?

315
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:23,480
Is Ryotsu here?

316
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:25,120
What's wrong, Chief?

317
00:17:25,740 --> 00:17:27,540
What do you mean, what's wrong?

318
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:29,900
I wasn't told it was worth 10 billion yen!

319
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:33,220
On top of that, some suspicious guy
is hanging around outside my house!

320
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:35,680
How am I supposed to keep
such a dangerous thing?

321
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:37,400
I'm giving it back. Right now.

322
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:37,720
Don't say that...

323
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:40,660
I have no one to rely on but you, Chief.

324
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,560
If it's you, Chief, no matter what happens,

325
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:44,980
I believe you'll keep the pot safe.

326
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:48,320
You're not the kind of man who'd
betray your subordinates' trust,

327
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,320
I know that.

328
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:53,360
and you're not one to break a promise
once you've agreed to keep something.

329
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:55,020
I know that well.

330
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:56,040
Exactly.

331
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:58,000
I always keep my promises.

332
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,360
That's right, that's right indeed.

333
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:01,620
As expected of you, Chief.

334
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:04,080
No, the best in Japan.
No, the best in the world.

335
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:10,460
Whoa!

336
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:11,740
My beads!

337
00:18:14,140 --> 00:18:15,320
Narrow escape!

338
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:18,380
Who left a banana peel lying around here?

339
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:22,000
Sorry. I was just a little hungry.

340
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,440
Hey, you!

341
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:27,560
Come on, Chief.
You don't think I did it on purpose, do you?

342
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:29,880
As if I'd ever do such a thing.

343
00:18:30,140 --> 00:18:32,940
If it got out, I couldn't pay for
it even if I worked my whole life.

344
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:34,400
I-I know.

345
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:38,780
About the old man from Tsukudajima,
since you're taking good care of it, Chief,

346
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:40,900
I told him he could rest easy.

347
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:42,840
Please keep it safe.

348
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:44,960
Ugh, you're so annoying!

349
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:53,500
The tsubo!

350
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:55,080
What on earth is this?

351
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:00,240
Alright, keep going!

352
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,820
H-hey, what do you think you're doing?

353
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:06,040
I'm asking what you're doing!

354
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:08,960
Isn't it obvious? It's road construction.

355
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:12,960
I'm asking why you're doing
construction in front of the police box!

356
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,840
Wait, the tsubo, the tsubo!

357
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:20,720
We haven't approved any construction.

358
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:22,060
Hurry up and move it.

359
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:24,120
Even if you say that to me...

360
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,940
Bro, I'll get another one!

361
00:19:27,180 --> 00:19:29,780
Anyway, don't do any construction here.

362
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,100
Hey, wait, stop!

363
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:35,940
Hey, hello?

364
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:38,120
What I said earlier was a mistake.

365
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:39,720
Yes, understood.

366
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:44,080
Sorry, I think we misunderstood.

367
00:19:44,840 --> 00:19:46,780
Once you get it, hurry up and go, alright?

368
00:19:50,660 --> 00:19:54,820
I'm really cornered now...
well then, time for the final touch.

369
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:04,480
Today has been a total disaster.
I shouldn't have said I'd look after it.

370
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:09,040
But it's not like I get to hold
a 10 billion yen pot very often.

371
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:20,240
What am I supposed to do?

372
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,700
Time... 10 billion...

373
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:23,520
That's it!

374
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:27,440
If it's model glue...

375
00:20:39,360 --> 00:20:42,600
This should be good as new now.

376
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,640
But why are there extra parts left over?

377
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:47,740
We're back from patrol.

378
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:52,220
Chief, what are you doing over here?

379
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:54,240
Well, nothing really.

380
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:57,220
Hey, Chief, what kind of glue did you use?

381
00:20:57,220 --> 00:21:00,240
Wait, why is there glue over here?

382
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:06,720
Speaking of which, I hear more and more adults
can't properly apologize when they do something wrong.

383
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:09,880
R-really? That's outrageous.

384
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:15,480
Especially the ones who break something entrusted to them and then try to play dumb.
They're the worst, aren't they?

385
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:17,680
Y-yeah, you're absolutely right.

386
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:22,000
It'd be nice if everyone were as
serious and honest as you, Chief.

387
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,980
Chief, you're not hiding
anything from me, are you?

388
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,160
N-no, nothing at all.

389
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:29,170
If you're going to apologize,
now's the time.

390
00:21:29,220 --> 00:21:32,140
I might forgive you, just this once.

391
00:21:32,140 --> 00:21:35,540
W-what are you talking about?
I-I have no idea.

392
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:39,200
You really didn't do anything?

393
00:21:41,420 --> 00:21:43,740
Oh no! The pot's cracked!

394
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:49,340
It's over! My life is finished!

395
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,440
Bucchan

396
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:51,160
What?

397
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:55,580
Ta-da! Big success! It was a prank camera!

398
00:21:58,360 --> 00:22:02,460
That's why it's a surprise camera!
Everything about the pot was nonsense!

399
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,460
What? Then what about this pot?

400
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:07,340
It's the 500-yen pot I
bought myself as a prop.

401
00:22:07,340 --> 00:22:09,660
As for the story about it
being worth 10 billion yen,

402
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:12,980
yes, that appraisal show was a video I made.

403
00:22:12,980 --> 00:22:15,060
The figure lurking around the house,

404
00:22:15,060 --> 00:22:16,180
that was me too.

405
00:22:16,180 --> 00:22:18,240
As for the pot suddenly breaking,

406
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:20,300
I broke it in advance,

407
00:22:20,300 --> 00:22:23,100
and stuck it back together with
glue that peels off over time.

408
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:25,380
I see. So that's how it was.

409
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:27,040
Yes, that's exactly how it was.

410
00:22:28,020 --> 00:22:30,620
Jirōzu, you good-for-nothing...

411
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:32,620
Why are you angry?

412
00:22:34,460 --> 00:22:42,400
Chief, come on, even so, you went too far.
Senpai, hey, Nakagawa, Reiko.

413
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:51,360
You hit my pressure point, didn't you, Ryo-chan?
The pot you bought, senpai, was something very valuable.

414
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:56,320
What? When I asked Grandpa,
that pot wasn't for sale.

415
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:58,440
I sold it by mistake.

416
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:00,220
Is that all?

417
00:23:00,220 --> 00:23:02,200
It's not just that.

418
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:03,720
Actually, that pot is

419
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:07,480
a phantom pot from China's Song dynasty.

420
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:10,040
Apparently it's worth
at least 50 billion yen.

421
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:12,340
50 billion.

422
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:13,880
That's right.

423
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:16,380
Not 10 billion, but 50 billion yen in value.

424
00:23:16,380 --> 00:23:18,240
It's truly a pot fit for a king.

425
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:19,880
So, what about the pot?

426
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,260
Where is that pot now?

427
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:30,400
Ahhhhh, the Manbaboroshi pot is 500

428
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:36,600
Pull yourself together!
Hey, this is 50 billion!

429
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:40,860
So you're saying I smashed
50 billion with my own hands?

430
00:23:43,940 --> 00:23:48,340
Ahhhhh, you're kidding me, Nakagawa, Reiko!

431
00:23:48,340 --> 00:23:50,020
I'm sorry, but...

432
00:23:50,020 --> 00:23:51,680
It's all true.

433
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,600
Serves you right.

434
00:23:55,580 --> 00:23:56,780
No way! It's a lie!

435
00:23:57,720 --> 00:24:01,420
Somebody tell me this
was a prank camera too!

436
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:20,360
Like someone was calling out,
after the rain had stopped

437
00:24:21,820 --> 00:24:27,220
walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand

438
00:24:28,060 --> 00:24:34,180
that strange feeling I had back then

439
00:24:35,380 --> 00:24:39,620
so on the tiles of the arcade street,

440
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:45,400
I tried walking only on the black ones

441
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:51,560
Everyone was a kid once,

442
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:53,700
but everyone's forgotten

443
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:57,700
the politicians with
their self-important faces,

444
00:24:57,700 --> 00:25:01,000
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow, too

445
00:25:01,530 --> 00:25:04,000
Try turning the corner,

446
00:25:04,620 --> 00:25:06,600
that corner over there

447
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:11,780
you'll meet everyone, everyone

448
00:25:12,340 --> 00:25:13,000
How much?

449
00:25:14,040 --> 00:25:16,460
There's a wall over there

450
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:19,740
Surely a wall there too

451
00:25:21,300 --> 00:25:24,980
Everyone, come to our town!

452
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:26,560
Thank you

453
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:31,780
Bonus season has rolled
around again this year,

454
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:34,080
and I'm the one being chased
by the shopping street crowd.

455
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:36,500
I escaped Kameari ahead of Shikubi,

456
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:38,480
since you can withdraw money anywhere.

457
00:25:38,480 --> 00:25:41,080
But the mountain village I finally reached

458
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:44,000
was an outrageous place where
delinquent livestock ran wild.

459
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,680
Next time: Bonus Battle 7!

460
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:47,740
See you then.

461
00:25:51,820 --> 00:25:54,100
Well, I'm sure there'll be a wall or two.

462
00:25:54,100 --> 00:25:59,300
Everyone, come visit our town!

463
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:00,900
Thank you.

